KPL/LSK

AUTHORED BY FARSIGHT. THIS IS NOT A NAIF PRODUCT.

The second half of ADR-016's `ci-kernel-override-canary`. Furnished AFTER
`farsight_authored.tls`, it overrides that kernel's leap-second table with a deliberately
different one, so that the two furnish orders produce **different geometry** rather than merely
different hashes.

That distinction is the whole point of the canary. Two orderings of the same files always produce
different `kernel_set_hash` values -- JCS preserves array order, so that is guaranteed by the
serialization and proves nothing about SPICE. The assertion worth making is that the ORDER
CHANGES THE ANSWER, which is what makes ADR-016's ordered-sequence identity earned rather than
assumed. If this file's values ever stopped differing from the other fixture's, the canary would
pass while testing nothing.

The table below is fictional: 40 leap seconds from 2015, not 36. No real epoch has this offset.
It is chosen to be obviously wrong so that a value computed under it can never be mistaken for a
physical result if it leaks into an output.

\begindata

DELTET/DELTA_T_A       =   32.184
DELTET/K               =    1.657D-3
DELTET/EB              =    1.671D-2
DELTET/M               = (  6.239996D0   1.99096871D-7 )

DELTET/DELTA_AT        = ( 40,   @2015-JUL-1
                           41,   @2017-JAN-1 )

\begintext

End of the FarSight-authored override fixture.
